BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:95278c29-1fc1-4437-8053-50a97a2b808a@kit.events
DTSTAMP:20261029T080022Z
SUMMARY:Vinyl Night with Little Horse
DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver:20260928T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver:20260928T210000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY
DESCRIPTION:Bring your records or play ours. Little Horse Vintage brings
  crates to buy from.\n\nMonday 28 September\, 5 to 9pm. Free to turn up\,
  no sign-up.\n\nWe are partnering with Little Horse Vintage\, a short walk
  on Main Street\, to host an evening playing choice selections as well as
  anything you bring in. Requests welcome.\n\nBring a record from home\,
  and if we play it\, your next beer is buy one get one free.\n\nLittle
  Horse Vintage is also providing records to sell as well as to play\, so
  bring a bit of cash if you want to dig through the crates.\n\nLittle
  Horse has been dealing in vintage vinyl\, books and stereo gear around
  Louisville and Boulder since 2004. Their shop is a short walk away at 820
  Main
  Street.\n\nhttps://www.thegravitybrewing.com/events/vinyl-night-with-litt
 le-horse
URL:https://www.thegravitybrewing.com/events/vinyl-night-with-little-horse
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aca12d14-44a8-41f8-bb44-447505beac33@kit.events
DTSTAMP:20261029T080022Z
SUMMARY:Commander Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/Denver:20261019T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Denver:20261019T203000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY
DESCRIPTION:Free Magic: The Gathering for all levels. Starter decks from
  Total Escape Games.\n\nCommander Night starts Monday\, October 19\, and
  then runs every Monday from 5:30 to 8:30pm. It's free to play\, and your
  first drink of the night is $1 off.\n\nWe're hosting it with Total Escape
  Games\, Broomfield's tabletop game store since 2009. Their calendar runs
  all week: Friday Night Magic\, prerelease weekends\, Warhammer\, D&D and
  more\, backed by a Discord community over 2\,000 strong. They're bringing
  starter decks\, so you can sit down and play without owning a single
  card.\n\nCommander is the multiplayer format of Magic: The Gathering\,
  usually four players to a table. Bring your own deck or borrow one of
  theirs. New players are welcome.\n\nTotal Escape Games: 6831 W. 120th
  Ave\, Suite C\, Broomfield.
  https://www.totalescapegames.com/\n\nhttps://www.thegravitybrewing.com/ev
 ents/mtg-commander-night
URL:https://www.thegravitybrewing.com/events/mtg-commander-night
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
